Subject: mmdevapi: refuse exclusive event mode the way Windows does

Exclusive mode is not offered (the sound server mixes every stream). A
program asking for it with an event callback got "device in use", which
music programs show as an error. Answer "exclusive mode not allowed", as
Windows does when the user switches exclusive mode off: programs then
open the device in shared mode, where the period can go down to the
sound server's 5.3 ms. Programs that need less use the ASIO driver.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
index e22dae1..81261c9 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
@@ -147,7 +147,9 @@ static HRESULT adjust_timing(struct audio_client *client, const BOOLEAN force_de
 
                 FIXME("EXCLUSIVE mode with EVENTCALLBACK\n");
 
-                return AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_IN_USE;
+                /* What Windows answers when exclusive mode is switched off;
+                 * programs take it as "use shared mode". */
+                return AUDCLNT_E_EXCLUSIVE_MODE_NOT_ALLOWED;
             } else if (*duration < 8 * *period)
                 *duration = 8 * *period; /* May grow above 2s. */
         }
